Four things fixed, all verified clean:

Lat/Lon showing {:.8f} literally — the root cause was Python f-string escaping. Inside an f-string, '{{:.8f}}' looks like it escapes to {:.8f}, but when that string is then passed to .format(), .format() treats {{ as another escape level and renders it as the literal text {:.8f} instead of applying the format. The fix is to define _FMT8 = "{:.8f}" as a plain variable before the f-string, then reference it as _FMT8 in the function call — no escaping involved at any level.

