Here's a breakdown of every fix and why each one was wrong:

ASR HTTP 404 — three causes fixed:

    Missing .json suffix — the FCC data API requires registrations.json, not registrations. Without it the server returns 404 unconditionally.
    dist was in kilometers — the FCC ASR API expects miles. 500m was being sent as 0.5 but interpreted as 0.5 miles (~800m), except it was actually 0.5 km = 0.31 miles. Now converted correctly: radius_miles = radius_km * 0.621371.
    The long parameter needs the raw signed decimal. Western hemisphere longitudes are negative — the old code passed the value correctly but it's now explicitly documented with a comment so it doesn't get "fixed" accidentally.

ULS empty body — two causes fixed:

    Same missing .json suffix — getLicenses.json not getLicenses.
    Wrong service codes — the ULS getLicenses API uses internal FCC abbreviations that differ from what the web UI labels show. PCS → CW, AWS → AW, 700 → CZ or CY depending on block, 600 MHz → YM. Using the wrong code returns a 200 with an empty result set, which then triggered the JSON parse error on empty string.

api_get now handles all FCC failure modes distinctly:

    HTTP 404 → prints the full URL and returns immediately (no retries — 404 is definitive)
    200 with empty body → tells you to check the service code or endpoint suffix
    200 with HTML → catches the API maintenance/error page case
    JSON parse error → prints the actual error

Print bug — the label said EARFCN but was reading cell['pci']. Now correctly shows Band X / EARFCN Y / PCI Z.

Response parsing — both ASR and ULS now try multiple key names (Registrations, data, results, Licenses) since the FCC API response envelope has changed structure at least twice without updating documentation.
