PCI/EARFCN values were swapped — the output showed EARFCN 242 / PCI 1000 but from your session data those are inverted. The root cause is that CellMapper's CSV export format has shifted between app versions — some versions put EARFCN at column 10 and PCI at column 11, opposite of what GNSS_AttackModel.ps1 expects. The fix is automatic: the script now checks whether the value labeled Cell_PCI is in the valid 3GPP PCI range (0–503). If it's above 503 it can only be an EARFCN, so the two values are swapped silently. A note in the session summary prints when this correction is applied.

